# Normalise line endings to LF on checkout, on every platform.
#
# Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF to CRLF when checking
# out, which breaks three things here that compare bytes rather than lines:
#
#   - golden/**            compared byte for byte against rendered output
#   - static/js/*.js       unwrapped by anchored regexes in the goja tests
#   - static/js/mermaid.min.js  pinned by sha256 in handler_test.go
#
# All three failed on the windows-latest CI runner until this file existed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The mermaid bundle is a vendored artifact, not source. Never transform it —
# its sha256 is asserted — and do not try to diff 5 MB of minified JavaScript.
static/js/mermaid.min.js -text -diff
